I implemented the node with only the `state-rw` import. I left out both operations requests: the node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. That gives it no filesystem access for `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and no HTTP capability for the metadata service. Adding either would need a separate grant in the node's `with` clause. The node's output is unaffected.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        // Only mark items as seen once the digest was actually published;
        // otherwise they should be reconsidered on the next run.
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                state_rw::put(id, "1");
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

